{
 "shapes": [
  {
   "id": "title",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 280,
   "y": 30,
   "width": 400,
   "height": 40,
   "text": "TCP three-way handshake",
   "fontSize": 36
  },
  {
   "id": "clientBox",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 90,
   "y": 110,
   "width": 210,
   "height": 70,
   "text": "Client",
   "fontSize": 28,
   "backgroundColor": "#E8F3FF",
   "strokeColor": "#2B6CB0"
  },
  {
   "id": "serverBox",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 660,
   "y": 110,
   "width": 210,
   "height": 70,
   "text": "Server",
   "fontSize": 28,
   "backgroundColor": "#EFFFF4",
   "strokeColor": "#2F855A"
  },
  {
   "id": "clientLine",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 195,
   "y": 190,
   "width": 0,
   "height": 380,
   "strokeColor": "#2B6CB0"
  },
  {
   "id": "serverLine",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 765,
   "y": 190,
   "width": 0,
   "height": 380,
   "strokeColor": "#2F855A"
  },
  {
   "id": "note",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 340,
   "y": 110,
   "width": 280,
   "height": 70,
   "text": "Before data flows,\nTCP agrees a connection.",
   "fontSize": 20
  },
  {
   "id": "synArrow",
   "type": "arrow",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 0,
   "height": 0,
   "fromId": "clientLine",
   "toId": "serverLine",
   "text": "1. SYN",
   "strokeColor": "#D69E2E"
  },
  {
   "id": "synAckArrow",
   "type": "arrow",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 0,
   "height": 0,
   "fromId": "serverLine",
   "toId": "clientLine",
   "text": "2. SYN-ACK",
   "strokeColor": "#805AD5"
  },
  {
   "id": "ackArrow",
   "type": "arrow",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 0,
   "height": 0,
   "fromId": "clientLine",
   "toId": "serverLine",
   "text": "3. ACK",
   "strokeColor": "#D69E2E"
  },
  {
   "id": "readyBox",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 340,
   "y": 525,
   "width": 280,
   "height": 70,
   "text": "Connection established\nReady for data",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "backgroundColor": "#FFF7D6",
   "strokeColor": "#B7791F"
  }
 ],
 "beats": [
  {
   "say": "Alright mate, TCP doesn't just start flinging data around like a dodgy hose; it does a quick handshake first, no dramas.",
   "reveal": [
    "title",
    "clientBox",
    "serverBox",
    "clientLine",
    "serverLine",
    "note"
   ],
   "emphasize": [
    "clientBox",
    "serverBox"
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "First up, the client sends a SYN, basically saying, 'Oi server, keen to open a connection?' Bloody simple start.",
   "reveal": [
    "synArrow"
   ],
   "emphasize": [
    "synArrow",
    "clientBox",
    "serverBox"
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "Then the server replies with SYN-ACK, which means, 'Yep, I heard ya, and I'm keen too.' Good on ya, server.",
   "reveal": [
    "synAckArrow"
   ],
   "emphasize": [
    "synAckArrow"
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "Finally, the client sends ACK back, saying, 'Sweet, I heard your reply.' That's the third step, and she's right to crack on.",
   "reveal": [
    "ackArrow"
   ],
   "emphasize": [
    "ackArrow"
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "After those three messages, the TCP connection is established, so both sides can start sending the actual data without that setup crap getting in the way.",
   "reveal": [
    "readyBox"
   ],
   "emphasize": [
    "synArrow",
    "synAckArrow",
    "ackArrow",
    "readyBox"
   ]
  }
 ]
}